H2: Known Faults - Alfa Romeo Giulietta
H3: Electrics: Sat-Nav, Air-Con and Stop-Start
P: MONITOR ú 2010-2020 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says there have been reports on newer cars of non-engine electrical problems, mostly relating to the sat-nav and air-con, as well as the stop-start system working intermittently.
H3: Gear Knob and Interior Trim
P: MINOR ú 2010-2020 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says the gearknob can work loose, occasionally even coming off, while the interior trim, particularly around the centre console area, has been known to become loose and make a noise. The RAC lists loose body kit trims and gear knobs that can rotate or come off among the small faults reported by owners of the 2010-2014 car.
H3: Blue&#x26;Me Bluetooth and Start&#x26;Stop
P: MINOR ú 2010-2014 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says owners of the 2010-2014 car reported a tendency for the Blue&#x26;Me infotainment system not to pair with Bluetooth handsets reliably, and Start&#x26;Stop systems that resolutely refuse to stop.
H3: MultiAir System
P: MONITOR ú 2014-2020 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says that issues with the MultiAir system are less common after revisions in 2014.
H3: Diesel Injectors, Clutch and Flywheel
P: MONITOR ú 2014-2020 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says injectors can fail, and the torque output can wear out clutches and flywheels, but that applies to most modern diesels.
H3: TCT Automatic Gearbox
P: CHECK ú 2014-2020 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says the TCT automatic gearbox can reportedly cause expensive bills with higher mileages.
H3: Boot Lock and Spare Wheel Well Water
P: CHECK ú 2010-2020 ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says the boot lock can fill up with water after heavy rain, leading to the mechanism seizing up and potentially the spare wheel well flooding.
H3: Rear Light Condensation
P: MINOR ú 2010-2020 ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says the rear light clusters have a habit of suffering from failed seals, which allows water in, causing annoying condensation on the glass in cold weather.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: Auto Express says a campaign launched in July 2015 was aimed at Giuliettas with the 2.0-litre MultiJet engine and a TCT gearbox, built up to May 2015. It says a chafing wiring loom could lead to problems with the transmission and potentially a loss of drive altogether.
P: DVSA's recall data lists these Giulietta recalls:
LI: The intercooler sleeve may detach.
LI: The wiring loom connected to the transmission oil pump may chafe against a support bracket and damage the wiring. Damaged wiring may cause loss of drive or adversely affect gear changes.
P: Any particular Giulietta can be checked for an open recall with our recall check .
H2: Reliability Survey Results
LI: In its 2023 study, What Car? put the Giulietta in 8th place in the family cars category with a score of 92%.
LI: What Car? says Alfa Romeo, as a brand, finished 12th out of 30 manufacturers, with an overall score of 82.7%.
LI: The RAC says the 2010-2014 Giulietta fared reasonably well in terms of reliability, with a strong score in customer satisfaction surveys.
LI: Carbuyer calls a 103rd-place finish for reliability disappointing and a 133rd-place result for build quality poor.
LI: Carbuyer says Alfa Romeo, as a brand, came ninth out of 30 manufacturers in 2020, a drop from its second-place finish in 2018.
LI: Auto Express says Alfa Romeo, as a brand, has seen improved scores in recent Driver Power surveys, but that newer cars such as the Giulia and Stelvio are propelling the firm up the charts, rather than older models like the Giulietta.
