H2: Known Faults - Alfa Romeo Giulia
H3: Electrical Faults
P: MONITOR ú Some cars ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says electrical gremlins were common, with complaints about warning lights, faulty sensors and frozen infotainment screens. The RAC's reviewer says they have come across quite a few electrical issues. Carbuyer says 28% of owners reported at least one fault within the first year of ownership, mostly related to the electrics. Autocar's nearly new guide says random unexplained events are common, and that re-flashing software updates and new connections are often the solution.
H3: Infotainment and Dashboard Screens
P: MONITOR ú Some cars ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says some owners have reported that the infotainment screen and the central dashboard screen have become dark and unresponsive, and that this requires a software update. What Car? says one reader noted repeated problems with the infotainment system freezing, requiring multiple visits to the dealer.
H3: Battery and Start-Stop
P: CHECK ú 2016-2022 ú Get a quote
P: In its review of the 2016-2022 Giulia, the RAC says a number of owners have had battery failures, which in some cases are prefaced by assistance module failures such as the start stop system ceasing to work.
H3: Engine Electronics and Limp Mode
P: CHECK ú 2016-2022 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC's 2016-2022 review says some owners have had issues with engine electronics, resulting in all kinds of issues ranging from the engine check light coming on to complete limp mode activation.
H3: Brakes and E-Brake
P: CHECK ú Some cars ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says brake issues were reported by owners. The RAC's reviewer says they also heard of problems with the E-brake system getting stuck, which needs to be released in the brake service mode on the infotainment screen.
H3: Suspension
P: CHECK ú Some cars ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says suspension noises were reported by owners. The RAC says it has come across a number of problems with the suspension and axles, which include issues with the drive mode selector causing the suspension to lock up. It adds that some owners have reported that the front suspension clunks over small bumps.
H3: Coolant Hose Clamps
P: CHECK ú Some cars ú Get a quote
P: Autocar says loose hose clamps, for example on the coolant pipes, can lead to leaks.
H3: Parts and Dealer Service
P: MINOR ú Some cars ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says a number of readers described delays in getting parts and inconsistent service from dealers. Autocar says some components can take an age to source.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several Giulia recalls, including these.
LI: On affected vehicles due to a production nonconformity the wiring harness leading to the headlamp ECU could become damaged by tyre interference with the wheel arch liner which could result in error messages being displayed and a loss of headlamp low beam functionality.
LI: Affected vehicles equipped with the option BRM (carbon ceramic matrix brakes) may face a braking management issue due to unexpected control unit signals.
LI: The automatic headlight position sensors may not have been calibrated and therefore the function does not comply with the requirements of ECE R48.
LI: Due to a production nonconformity there may be the possibility of a fuel leak from the fuel pressure and temperature sensor.
LI: There is a possibility of the rear brake discs having micro-cracks.
LI: The seats may not lock in the correct position.
LI: Fuel leakages may occur and fumes may form inside the passenger compartment.
P: To see if a Giulia has an open recall, use our recall check .
