H2: Known Faults - Alfa Romeo Stelvio
H3: 12-Volt Battery
P: MONITOR ú 2017 on ú Get a quote
P: What Car? lists the 12-volt battery as the most common fault in the 2017-present Stelvio, at 16%. The RAC says a number of owners have had battery failures, which in some cases are prefaced by assistance module failures such as the start stop system ceasing to work. Autocar says battery failures aren't uncommon, and an owner told Autocar that one day the battery failed and, while it didn't stop them using the car, it did throw up some errors.
H3: Suspension and Drive Mode Selector
P: MONITOR ú 2017-2022 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says it has come across a number of problems with the suspension and axles on the 2017-2022 Stelvio, which include issues with the drive mode selector causing the suspension to lock up. It also says some owners have reported that the front suspension clunks over small bumps.
H3: Engine Electronics
P: MONITOR ú 2017-2022 ú Get a quote
P: According to the RAC, some owners of the 2017-2022 Stelvio have had issues with engine electronics, resulting in all kinds of issues ranging from the engine check light coming on to complete limp mode activation.
H3: Coil Packs
P: CHECK ú 2017-2023 ú Get a quote
P: Autocar says that on the 2017-2023 Stelvio, misfires or reduced performance can be caused by a faulty coil pack, and that replacements are expensive.
H3: Coolant Leaks
P: CHECK ú 2017-2023 ú Get a quote
P: Autocar says damaged hoses or a broken radiator can cause coolant leaks and overheating on the 2017-2023 Stelvio.
H2: Reliability Surveys
P: In the 2025 What Car? Reliability Survey, the Stelvio finished in 66th place out of 76 family SUVs with a score of 85.3%, which What Car? calls a poor performance.
P: Alfa Romeo owners told What Car? that 33% of their Alfa Romeo cars suffered a glitch, and some issues were slow and costly to put right.
P: Autocar says a third of the Alfa Romeo Stelvio models it reported on went wrong, and a third of faulty cars were in the workshop for more than a week.
P: Carbuyer says owners love the way their cars look and drive, but reliability seems to be a weakness: some 28.6% of Alfa owners reported at least one fault within the first year of ownership, in the 2020 Driver Power survey.
P: Auto Express says the Stelvio boasts strong crash-test results, with positive customer feedback on brand performance.
