H2: Known Faults - Alfa Romeo Tonale
H3: Reliability Survey Results
P: MONITOR ú 2022 on ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says the Tonale lets the side down, with a rating of 85.4% and a fault rate of 47%. Of Alfa Romeo as a brand, What Car? says the Italian car maker has upped its game. Parkers says Alfa's reliability record isn't good but is improving, and that the Tonale is new to the UK market, so it is too soon to call it on reliability. Carbuyer says the Tonale might finally be the car to shake Alfa Romeo's poor reputation for reliability. Carbuyer also says the percentage of Alfa Romeo owners who reported issues was slightly higher than average at 28%. Auto Express says most people haven't had significant problems, and what they have had is certainly no worse than you could experience elsewhere.
H3: Speed Limit Recognition and Cameras
P: MONITOR ú 2022 on ú Get a quote
P: Autocar ran a Tonale plug-in hybrid as a long-term test car in 2024. It says the randomly faulty speed limit recognition system is off-putting even if you know it's wrong, and that the system can be wildly inaccurate. Fleet News, in its long-term test of a plug-in hybrid, reported a "camera blinded" message in bright sunshine and a similar "camera disabled" message when it was raining.
H3: Warning Messages and Electrical Bugs
P: MONITOR ú 2022 on ú Get a quote
P: Fleet News says that since its long-term Tonale's service, the car is showing fewer of what appear to be unnecessary warning messages, though that is not to say it has stopped them completely. Fleet News adds that there have been some electrical bugs detailed in previous tests.
H3: Infotainment and Proximity Sensors
P: CHECK ú 2022 on ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express lists over-enthusiastic proximity sensors, infotainment systems that can shut down and collision warnings on clear roads on the Tonale. It says software updates are key.
H3: Hybrid Systems at Low Speeds
P: MINOR ú 2022 on ú Get a quote
P: In its verdict, published in June 2023, Parkers says the steering is numb and the hybrid systems are clunky at low speeds.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several Tonale recalls, including these.
LI: Certain vehicles may have been equipped with an open roof anti-pinch system which does not operate according to specification.
LI: Affected vehicles may have a non-conforming tightening torque applied to the 12V battery recharge cable the two ground cables and the two HV (high voltage) connectors.
LI: Affected vehicles may have been fitted with a faulty 48-volt battery.
LI: Brake lights may remain illuminated when cruise control engaged.
P: Enter the registration in our recall check to see whether a car has an open recall.
