H2: Known Faults - Alfa Romeo MiTo
H3: What Car? Reliability Verdict
P: MONITOR ú 2008-present cars ú Get a quote
P: What Car?, on its page for the Mito 2008-present, says most problems relate to non-engine electrics. It reports timing chain issues on the Multijet engines, an engine management light that can come on, leaks from the transmission oil, power steering failures and some gearbox issues.
P: It also says interior trim can creak and rattle. The Mito did not feature in What Car?'s most recent reliability survey, but previous surveys have found it in the bottom half of the table, with the problems it lists.
H3: Hard First Gear
P: MONITOR ú Auto Express buyer's guide ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express, in its used buyer's guide, says first gear can be hard to select, especially on low-mileage cars and before the gearbox has warmed up.
H3: RAC Drive Reliability Verdict
P: MONITOR ú 2014-2018 cars ú Get a quote
P: RAC Drive, reviewing the MiTo (2014 - 2018), says the car has a reliability record that is at the lower end of acceptable. It also says the engines tend to be solid and rustproofing is excellent.
H3: Driver Power 2016 Placings
P: MONITOR ú Auto Express survey ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says the MiTo scraped into its 2016 Driver Power satisfaction survey in 148th place. It calls reliability (145th), build quality (145th) and ride quality (150th) particularly disappointing.
H3: Paint Chipping and Scratching
P: MINOR ú Some owners ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says some MiTo owners have had issues with their paint chipping and scratching easily.
H3: Parkers Owner Reports
P: CHECK ú One owner's report each ú Get a quote
P: One Parkers owner of a 0.9 TB TwinAir Sprint wrote that they love Alfa styling, but that the car's reliability combined with the customer service they received has put them off ever risking another. That owner wrote that within the first six weeks the engine management light had come on twice and the car was back with the dealer.
P: One Parkers owner of a 1.4 16V Turismo wrote that the alternator seized, so the electrics all failed once.
P: One Parkers owner of a 1.4 TB MultiAir Distinctive with the TCT gearbox wrote of several annoying small issues. They listed a noisy and sometimes a little daft TCT gearbox that would almost stall the car when coming to a stop under certain conditions, a petrol smell in the cabin at idle, a rattly wastegate and a driver's seat that would recline on its own.
P: One Parkers owner of a 1.6 JTDM Veloce wrote that a sensor lit on the dash and turned out to be a filter clog, and that they needed to drive the car more. That owner also wrote that the ride isn't good, with lots of bangs and rattles especially over uneven roads.
P: Engines, gearboxes and trims by period are in our Alfa Romeo MiTo parts guide . Before you view a car, put its registration into our recall check to see whether a DVSA safety recall is open.
H2: Breakdown cover
P: If a fault stops the car on the road, breakdown cover sends help to you. Compare two UK providers and check what each policy includes.
P: We earn a commission if you buy cover through these links, at no cost to you ( how we're paid ).
H2: Alfa Romeo MiTo MOT results in 2025
P: There were 17,227 MOT tests of the Alfa Romeo MiTo in 2025. 39.3% failed first time, against 27.7% for all cars. Older cars fail more often, so the fairer comparison is by age:
H3: What they failed on
LI: Suspension : 14.8% of tests (all cars 9.0%). Shock absorber prices
LI: Lamps, reflectors and electrical equipment : 12.6% of tests (all cars 10.6%). Headlight bulb prices by type
LI: Brakes : 10.7% of tests (all cars 6.2%). Brake pad prices , brake disc prices
LI: Tyres : 7.7% of tests (all cars 6.2%)
LI: Noise, emissions and leaks : 6.4% of tests
P: Initial MOT tests in Great Britain, 2025, from DVSA's anonymised MOT data; fail rate as DVSA calculates it (fails plus faults fixed during the test). Results cover every car recorded under the model name, so the older age bands can include earlier generations of it. Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0. MOT pass rates for every model and how they're worked out .
