H2: Frequently asked questions
P: RAC Drive says the MiTo has a reliability record at the lower end of acceptable, while adding that the engines tend to be solid and rustproofing is excellent. What Car? says previous surveys found the car in the bottom half of its table.
P: What Car? says most problems relate to non-engine electrics. It lists timing chain issues on the Multijet engines, the engine management light coming on, transmission oil leaks, power steering failures and some gearbox issues. Auto Express adds that first gear can be hard to select and that some owners have had paint chipping and scratching easily.
P: Auto Express says the MiTo scraped into its 2016 Driver Power satisfaction survey in 148th place. Reliability and build quality were both 145th and ride quality was 150th.
